#!/usr/bin/env sh
# EDIT-FROZEN DISPATCHER (plan 2576) — do NOT add gate logic here.
#
# The gate battery lives in scripts/hooks/pre-push.sh. This file exists only to
# dispatch to it, because `.husky/**` is a path an unattended cloud drain can
# never Edit/Write (the harness safetyCheck has no approver and the session
# hangs until the window dies — plans 2197/2213). Keeping the logic under
# scripts/ makes every future gate plan cloud-eligible; keeping THIS file
# stable means it never needs another edit. Add gates to the runner instead.
#
# SOURCED, not exec'd: `.` runs the runner in THIS shell, so its `exit` codes,
# its `trap … EXIT` cleanup and its single-read stdin capture keep the exact
# semantics husky's `sh -e "$s"` wrapper had before the move.
#
# Resolved RELATIVE TO CWD, not from `$0`, and not via git:
#   - git runs hooks from the top level of the working tree, and the runner
#     already depends on that invariant in 42 places (`node scripts/*.mjs`),
#     as does husky's own wrapper (`PATH="node_modules/.bin:$PATH"`). So this
#     adds no assumption the battery did not already make.
#   - `${0%/*}` is WRONG on Windows: Git Bash hands this hook a backslash path
#     (C:\…\.husky\pre-push), which contains no `/`, so the expansion strips
#     nothing and yields `<file>/../scripts/…`.
#   - `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` is WRONG under test: this hook's own name-paired test
#     runs this hook with a FAKE git on PATH whose catch-all answers with exit 0
#     and no output, resolving the runner to an empty path.
. ./scripts/hooks/pre-push.sh
